    "rsv_0246": "Endpoints",
    "rsv_0247": "Enlarging a small image invents pixels that were never there, so it turns soft and blurry. Start from the largest original you have, and scale down to the size you need.",
    "rsv_0248": "Enter a battle certificate number. Full verification against issued records arrives with Phase 3.",
    "rsv_0249": "Enter a certificate registration number. This page checks the format only — full verification against issued records arrives with Phase 3.",
    "rsv_0250": "Error codes",
    "rsv_0251": "Errors return a standard JSON error response with a code and a message.",
    "rsv_0252": "Every DoKit tool runs in your browser — no signup, no uploads, no watermark.",
    "rsv_0253": "Every finished session on this device, newest first. Nothing is uploaded anywhere.",
    "rsv_0254": "Every save in a lossy format (JPEG, WebP) costs quality. Do all your edits first, then save once at the end, in the format you'll actually publish.",
    "rsv_0256": "Everything runs on your device. Pick a tool and start — no account, no waiting.",
    "rsv_0257": "Exact pixels",
    "rsv_0258": "Exact-KB targets",
    "rsv_0259": "Exam & admission photos in the exact size your board wants.",
    "rsv_0260": "Experiments and variants.",
    "rsv_0221": "DoKit may change, add, or retire tools over time. Free basic tools will not be taken away or downgraded.",
    "rsv_0222": "DoKit started with a simple frustration: everyday online tools were stuffed with pop-up ads, demanded an account before doing anything useful, or quietly uploaded your files to a server you never asked about. So we built the opposite. Every DoKit tool runs entirely on your device, inside your browser. Your photos are resized on your phone. Your words are counted on your laptop. There is no server to breach, because your files never leave your hands.",
    "rsv_0224": "DoKit runs without any third-party library, and a zip library would break that promise. Separate download tools keep it fast and self-contained.",
    "rsv_0226": "DoKit — Free Online Tools",
    "rsv_0227": "DoKit's free tools are provided as-is, for personal and professional use. You are responsible for the content you process with them and for checking outputs before you rely on them.",
    "rsv_0228": "DoKit's image tools saved me hours. No upload, no waiting — everything happens instantly in the browser.",
    "rsv_0230": "Download PNG",
    "rsv_0231": "Download as PDF",
    "rsv_0232": "Download as PDF opens your browser's print dialog — choose \"Save as PDF\". Official QR-verified certificates arrive with the backend in Phase 3.",
    "rsv_0233": "Download photo",
    "rsv_0234": "Download the compressed image at or under the target.",
    "rsv_0235": "Each resize-and-save round loses a little quality. Keep your original safe, and always produce the resized copy from it — never resize an already-resized file.",
