    "guide_case_cta": "Open Case Converter",
    "guide_case_faq1_a": "It flips every letter's case — uppercase becomes lowercase and vice versa. Mostly for fun or stylized text.",
    "guide_case_faq2_a": "Each part of a hyphenated word is capitalized (e.g. “well-known” → “Well-Known”).",
    "guide_case_faq3_a": "No — conversion happens entirely in your browser. Your text never leaves your device.",
    "guide_case_faq4_a": "Yes. Urdu script has no uppercase/lowercase, so it stays as-is while any English words in the mix are converted.",
    "guide_case_h1": "How to convert text case",
    "guide_case_rel1_d": "UPPER, lower, Title Case and more.",
    "guide_case_steps_h": "Steps",
    "guide_case_tagline": "Fix ALL-CAPS headings, lowercase SHOUTING, and format titles perfectly — six case styles, one click each.",
    "guide_case_tip1": "Title Case is for headings — it capitalizes every major word, perfect for article and video titles.",
    "guide_case_tip2": "Sentence case fixes SHOUTING — paste ALL-CAPS text and get clean, readable sentences.",
    "guide_case_tip3": "Works with Urdu text too — Urdu script has no case, so it passes through unchanged while English words convert.",
    "guide_compress_h1": "How to compress images",
    "guide_convimg_cta": "Open Image Converter",
    "guide_convimg_faq1_a": "Photos: JPG or WebP. Graphics with transparency: PNG or WebP. Smallest web files: WebP.",
    "guide_convimg_faq2_a": "JPG and WebP are lossy — converting from PNG can lose a little detail. PNG output is always lossless.",
    "guide_convimg_faq3_a": "Convert them to WebP instead — it keeps animation at much smaller file sizes.",
    "guide_convimg_faq4_a": "No. Conversion happens entirely in your browser; nothing leaves your device.",
    "guide_convimg_h1": "How to convert image formats",
    "guide_convimg_rel1_d": "Convert between PNG, JPEG, and WebP.",
    "guide_convimg_rel2_d": "Shrink file size without visible quality loss.",
    "guide_convimg_rel3_d": "Change image dimensions in pixels or percent.",
    "guide_convimg_tagline": "Switch any image between JPG, PNG and WebP in seconds — smaller files, wider compatibility, zero uploads.",
    "guide_convimg_tip1": "WebP is the modern default — 25–35% smaller than JPEG at the same quality, supported by all modern browsers.",
    "guide_convimg_tip2": "Keep PNG for graphics with sharp lines, text or transparency — JPG will blur edges.",
    "guide_convimg_tip3": "Convert before compressing when targeting tiny file sizes — the right format does half the work.",
    "guide_idx_card1_t": "How to resize images",
    "guide_words_cta": "Open Word Counter",
    "guide_words_faq1_a": "No — counting happens entirely in your browser. Your text never leaves your device.",
    "guide_words_faq2_a": "Sequences of letters/numbers separated by spaces or punctuation. Hyphenated words count as one.",
    "guide_words_faq3_a": "Copy the text out of the document and paste it into the counter — formatting is ignored, only text is counted.",
    "guide_words_h1": "How to count words",
    "guide_words_rel1_d": "Live word, character, and reading-time stats.",
    "guide_words_tagline": "Instant word counts, reading time and keyword stats for essays, articles, captions and scripts.",
    "guide_words_tip1": "Reading time ≈ words ÷ 200. Speaking time is slower — about 130 words per minute.",
    "guide_words_tip2": "Watch keyword stuffing. If one word dominates the top-10 list, vary your vocabulary.",
    "guide_words_tip3": "Works with Urdu text too. Paste Urdu script and get accurate counts.",
